	(text "D7 + Q2: with 5 V present VSYS comes through D7 and Q2 is off;\nwithout it Q2 turns on and the cell feeds VSYS. The charger never carries the load.\nVBAT_SENSE = VBAT / 2 (1M/1M, ~2 uA). RAIL_EN low (default, R21) = both rails off.\n+5V_SW only exists while USB or 12 V is present (no boost from the cell)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 654.05 165.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "24150720-77dc-5abd-958b-75ffad1569e5")
	)
	(text "Pull-ups are on +3V3_SW, so nothing back-powers sensors when the rail is off.\nFirmware must switch +3V3_SW on before ANY I2C traffic, including relay changes:\nthe TCA9534 (on always-on 3V3) holds its outputs meanwhile (D20). OLED shares the bus."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 287.02 331.47 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "29ced190-c468-5866-8275-bf5b0b8d158f")
	)
	(text "SYSTEM POWER: LOAD SHARING, 3.3 V LDO, SWITCHED RAILS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 634.748 68.455 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "2c4c3751-a0dd-51fb-a1ec-be974946822a")
	)
	(text "ESP32-C6 / C3 MODULE"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 48.0083 215.775 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "39ea4d9e-520f-59ae-874e-177f75e04792")
	)
	(text "PROG: I = 1200 / R. 4.7k = 255 mA; bridge JP1 (2.35k) = 510 mA (D12).\nTEMP: JP2 bridged disables the NTC input. For a cell NTC, cut JP2 and fit\nR11 + J3 with values from the TP4056 datasheet (D27).\nJ4 (JST-PH): pin 1 = cell -, pin 2 = cell +. JST-PH polarity is not standardised:\ncheck each cell before connecting (D28).\nProtection (DW01A + FS8205A) sits in the cell's negative lead: board GND is the pack's P-."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 485.14 76.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "43b5398f-c118-5679-9944-effff9db3b75")
	)
	(text "VALVE DRIVERS (ULN2803A, TWO CHANNELS PER VALVE)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 47.8871 383.415 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "52b670ae-a665-515a-868e-e9291cd2a212")
	)
	(text "SENSOR PORTS: I2C, OLED, GPIO"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 266.0853 215.775 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "6d8727e9-fa90-5d4c-92ca-2ef0327100ab")
	)
	(text "USB-C INPUT"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 46.99 68.7173 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "73bd02d7-4bcf-55cc-b403-aea920649573")
	)
	(text "DI is tied low: the driver only ever sends 0, gated by TX through Q9.\nA 1 (and idle) is held by the 680R bias pair. Fine for Modbus at 9600 baud;\nmarginal with termination at both cable ends (D21). Bridge JP3 at a bus end.\nTransceiver, bias and pull-ups are on +3V3_SW, so RS485 is off with the rail."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 412.75 326.39 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "77aa2d00-f49b-53d7-9bec-ccdcecfc705b")
	)
	(text "TCA9534 pins start as inputs: the ULN2803A's internal input resistors then hold every\nvalve off until firmware drives P0-P3 (D16). Address 0x20 (A0-A2 low). P0-P3 high = valve on.\nEach output drives two Darlingtons in parallel (D68). Valves: 12 V DC, up to ~0.35 A, one at a\ntime - the SOP-18 package limits this, not the channels (D70). Not for pumps or latching valves.\nFLYBACK (D69): COM must be on the same +12V as the valves' V+ pins, after D1. A valve wired to\nany other supply loses its clamp and the Darlington avalanches at turn-off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 81.28 486.41 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "9ae0a48f-d590-5e44-8551-fc3af0e3066d")
	)
	(text "12 V INPUT, PROTECTION & 5 V BUCK"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 237.49 69.2617 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a88e0c4b-5809-5d11-9d24-60dc8aef5176")
	)
	(text "Pads marked [C6]/[C3] differ between the two modules (D15, D18).\nEverything essential uses pads that work on both; BTN2 and GPIO_A/B work\nonly with a C6. SW2 is BOOT and BTN1 (IO9 strap). IO8/IO9 must be high at reset.\nC17/C18 close to module pin 3."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 64.77 356.87 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ae473fea-3f70-586a-acfa-234a4ab737a5")
	)
	(text "CC1/CC2: 5.1k each to GND (USB-C sink, 5 V only).\nFit R3/R4 for an ESP32-C6 module, R5/R6 (DNP) for a C3 module:\nthe two modules have USB on different pads (DECISIONS D15/D19)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 57.15 156.21 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "e3644b75-1df4-5264-9121-ad4571899bba")
	)
	(text "LI-ION CHARGER & CELL PROTECTION"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 475.4831 68.09 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "e6a90acb-2b78-557b-a3e5-15186c5fa48a")
	)
	(text "D2 blocks reverse polarity; D3 (SMAJ15A) clamps surges. 15 V max input.\nV12_SENSE = 12 V x 100k/660k: 2.27 V at 15 V, inside the ADC range (D23).\nAP63205: fixed 5 V out. L1/C6/C7 to be checked against the datasheet (D25)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 242.57 130.81 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "e6e47502-043e-5795-8843-a13d8256beef")
	)
	(text "RS485 (DIRECTION FROM TX)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 384.0139 215.775 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ed0f6a92-58d3-5ebe-bed5-7efa8b2b36ac")
	)
